BasedOnStyle: Google
IndentWidth: 2
# 120, not Google's 80. The 80 cap was the only thing forcing a one-line
# accessor -- `const std::string& Channel::getName() const { return _name; }`
# and its ninety-odd siblings -- to break across three lines, which reads
# worse than the thing it was protecting. At 120 every such definition in the
# tree fits on its line (measured: 121 of them, up from 96 at 80), and
# AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine below is what actually collapses them.
#
# clang-format never emits a line past this limit, so CPPLINT.cfg's
# linelength must hold the SAME number or the two gates disagree and
# `make norm` fails on files `make norm-fix` just wrote.
ColumnLimit: 120
SortIncludes: true
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: All
DerivePointerAlignment: false
